{"abstract":"Lead generation refers to the identification of potential topics (the ‘leads’) of importance for journalists to report on. In this article we present μXL, a new lead generation tool based on a microservice architecture that includes a component of explainable AI. μXL collects and stores historical and real-time data from web sources, like Google Trends, and generates current and future leads. Leads are produced by a novel engine for hypothetical reasoning based on temporal logical rules, which can identify propositions that may hold depending on the outcomes of future events. This engine also supports additional features that are relevant for lead generation, such as user-defined predicates (allowing useful custom atomic propositions to be defined as Java functions) and negation (needed to specify and reason about leads characterized by the absence of specific properties). Our microservice architecture is designed using state-of-the-art methods and tools for API design and implementation, namely API patterns and the Jolie programming language. Thus, our development provides an additional validation of their usefulness in a new application domain (journalism). We also carry out an empirical evaluation of our tool.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Kostopoulou, Sofia","Montesi, Fabrizio","Vistrup, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-783341"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Vistrup, Jonas"],"keyword":["Explainable AI","Jolie","Lead generation","Microservices"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"μxl explainable lead generation with microservices and hypothetical answers","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00607-024-01321-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-783341","identifier":[{"id":"85199443562","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-80406493-fdec-4881-b084-62dd5e72d47f"],"keyword":["68T27","Explainable AI","Jolie","Lead generation","Microservices"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-357F06C2A29DEA73E425570C63C9A5E3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00607-024-01321-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/275834011/s00607-024-01321-x.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity and Programming Languages"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofia","key":"kostopouloupau","last":"Kostopoulou","locid":"fd6c9471-6ddd-4538-b203-0a46a76aa5ae","name":"Kostopoulou, Sofia","orcid":"0000-0002-5557-1295","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"vistruppau","last":"Vistrup","locid":"59f038f5-55e6-4339-bd05-1aa06b08971c","name":"Vistrup, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-7704-3656","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00607-024-01321-x","issn":["0010485X","03448029"],"issn_org":["0010485X"],"issue":"11","journal":"Computing","pages":"3419-3445","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Computing","volume":"106"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85199443562"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-80406493-fdec-4881-b084-62dd5e72d47f"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"μXL : explainable lead generation with microservices and hypothetical answers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-783341","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Answers to continuous queries over data streams are often delayed until some relevant input arrives through the data stream. These delays may turn answers when they arrive, obsolete to users who sometimes have to make decisions with no help whatsoever. Therefore, it can be useful to provide hypothetical answers—“given the current information, it is possible that X will become true at time t”—instead of no information at all. In this work, we present a semantics for queries and corresponding answers that cover such hypothetical answers, together with an incremental online algorithm for updating the set of facts that are consistent with the currently available information. Our framework also works in a language supporting negation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Gaspar, Graça","Nunes, Isabel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-782766"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lisbon"],"keyword":["Hypothetical reasoning","Stream reasoning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hypothetical answers to continuous queries over data streams","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3688845","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-782766","identifier":[{"id":"85208231028","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-0e04f505-c067-4639-9a02-867c73b78dda"],"keyword":["continuous query answering","hypothetical reasoning","stream reasoning","temporal Datalog"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B1F422003BFAC82CBC3AF9E0418FCB16"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3688845","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/276854443/3688845.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Graça","key":"gasparpau","last":"Gaspar","name":"Gaspar, Graça","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Isabel","key":"nunespau","last":"Nunes","name":"Nunes, Isabel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3688845","issn":["15293785","1557945X"],"issn_org":["15293785"],"issue":"4","journal":"ACM Transactions on Computational Logic","paperid":"25","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Transactions on Computational Logic","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208231028"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-0e04f505-c067-4639-9a02-867c73b78dda"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Hypothetical Answers to Continuous Queries Over Data Streams","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-782766","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Approximation Fixpoint Theory (AFT) is an abstract framework based on lattice theory that unifies semantics of different non-monotonic logic. AFT has revealed itself to be applicable in a variety of new domains within knowledge representation. In this work, we present a formalisation of the key constructions and results of AFT in the Coq theorem prover, together with a case study illustrating its application to propositional logic programming.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bogaerts, Bart","Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-750524"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"country":["Belgium"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Free University of Brussels"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"approximation fixpoint theory in coq with an application to logic programming","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85195935389","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-750524","identifier":[{"id":"85195935389","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-6655ba65-a208-4d19-81db-1ce83418d86a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C56BA898EFBF0CE691EAD338C2180374"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"be","key":"free university of brussels","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Free University of Brussels","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University 