"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lovro","key":"lugovicpau","last":"Lugovic","locid":"2fe35d95-917c-470f-b2ed-c1c5f4acfcac","name":"Lugović, Lovro","name_org":"Lugovic, Lovro","orcid":"0000-0001-9684-9567","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"peressottipau","last":"Peressotti","locid":"afca1964-ceda-46fa-b7c7-f6e77e401024","name":"Peressotti, Marco","orcid":"0000-0002-0243-0480","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-7cf40e9e-e4e9-40a7-bc5f-f9c4c9dbf5f8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Choreographic Programming in Coq","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-685201","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Choreographic programming is a paradigm where developers write the global specification (called choreography) of a communicating system, and then a correct-by-construction distributed implementation is compiled automatically. Unfortunately, it is possible to write choreographies that cannot be compiled, because of issues related to an agreement property known as knowledge of choice. This forces programmers to reason manually about implementation details that may be orthogonal to the protocol that they are writing. Amendment is an automatic procedure for repairing uncompilable choreographies. We present a formalisation of amendment from the literature, built upon an existing formalisation of choreographic programming. However, in the process of formalising the expected properties of this procedure, we discovered a subtle counterexample that invalidates the original published and peer-reviewed pen-and-paper theory. We discuss how using a theorem prover led us to both finding the issue, and stating and proving a correct formulation of the properties of amendment.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Montesi, Fabrizio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-690948"],"event":{"end":"2023-08-04","place":"Bialystok, pl","start":"2023-07-31","title":"14th International Conference on Interactive Theorem Proving, ITP 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Montesi, Fabrizio"],"keyword":["Choreographic Programming","Compilation","Program Repair","Theorem proving"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"now it compiles certified automatic repair of uncompilable protocols","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ITP.2023.11","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding This work was partially supported by Villum Fonden, grants no. 29518 and 50079, and the Independent Research Fund Denmark, grant no. 0135-00219."],"id":"S01-000.00-690948","identifier":[{"id":"85168767662","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-1fa2cf75-1c4e-4fdf-a51d-5eff89c9d931"],"keyword":["choreographic programming","compilation","program repair","theorem proving"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D6807D82483B5EDB28027545F7131E6D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/239082776/LIPIcs_ITP_2023_11.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ITP.2023.11","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity and Programming Languages","SDU, Faculty of Science, SDU Climate Cluster"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Adam","key":"naumowiczpedh","last":"Naumowicz","name":"Naumowicz, Adam","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rene","key":"thiemannpedh","last":"Thiemann","name":"Thiemann, Rene","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.itp.2023.11","eisbn":["9783959772846"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"14th International Conference on Interactive Theorem Proving, ITP 2023","volume":"268"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168767662"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1fa2cf75-1c4e-4fdf-a51d-5eff89c9d931"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Now It Compiles! Certified Automatic Repair of Uncompilable Protocols","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-690948","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Choreographic programming is a paradigm for concurrent and distributed software, whereby descriptions of the intended communications (choreographies) are automatically compiled into distributed code with strong safety and liveness properties (e.g., deadlock-freedom). Recent efforts tried to combine the theories of choreographic programming and higher-order functional programming, in order to integrate the benefits of the former with the modularity of the latter. However, they do not offer a satisfactory theory of compilation compared to the literature, because of important syntactic and semantic shortcomings: compilation is not modular (editing a part might require recompiling everything) and the generated code can perform unexpected global synchronisations. In this paper, we find that these shortcomings are not mere coincidences. Rather, they stem from genuine new challenges posed by the integration of choreographies and functions: knowing which participants are involved in a choreography becomes nontrivial, and divergence in applications requires rethinking how to prove the semantic correctness of compilation. We present a novel theory of compilation for functional choreographies that overcomes these challenges, based on types and a careful design of the semantics of choreographies and distributed code. The result: a modular notion of compilation, which produces code that is deadlock-free and correct (it operationally corresponds to its source choreography).","author_count":7,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Graversen, Eva","Lugović, Lovro","Montesi, Fabrizio","Peressotti, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-690980"],"event":{"end":"2023-07-21","place":"Seattle, us","start":"2023-07-17","title":"37th European Conference on Object-Oriented Programming, ECOOP 2023","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"keyword":["Calculus","Choreographies","Concurrency","Type systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modular compilation for higher order functional choreographies","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ECOOP.2023.7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-690980","identifier":[{"id":"85168897183","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-2d1b6df3-ce26-4f73-82fb-76b44360245d"],"keyword":["Choreographies","Concurrency","Type Systems","λ-calculus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-7A0E20EFCA4E38F392991956082F869F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ECOOP.2023.7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/239079934/LIPIcs_ECOOP_2023_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity and Programming Languages","SDU, Faculty of Science, SDU Climate Cluster"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"graversenpau","last":"Graversen","locid":"1a2ccb3c-832d-46ea-8d84-6f1e0f0da3dc","name":"Graversen, Eva","orcid":"0000-0002-9430-4907","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lovro","key":"lugovićpau","last":"Lugović","locid":"2fe35d95-917c-470f-b2ed-c1c5f4acfcac","name":"Lugović, Lovro","orcid":"0000-0001-9684-9567","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"peressottipau","last":"Peressotti","locid":"afca1964-ceda-46fa-b7c7-f6e77e401024","name":"Peressotti, Marco","orcid":"0000-0002-0243-0480","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ali","key":"karimpedh","last":"Karim","name":"Karim, Ali","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Salvaneschi","key":"guidopedh","last":"Guido","name":"Guido, Salvaneschi","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.ecoop.2023.7","isbn":["9783959772815"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl-Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"37th European Conference on Object-Oriented Programming (ECOOP 2023)","volume":"263"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168897183"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2d1b6df3-ce26-4f73-82fb-76b44360245d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Modular Compilation for Higher-Order Functional Choreographies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-690980","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Choreographic programming is an emerging programming paradigm for concurrent and distributed systems, where developers write the communications that should be enacted and a compiler then automatically generates a distributed implementation. Currently, the most advanced incarnation of the paradigm is Choral, an object-oriented choreographic programming language that targets Java. Choral deviated significantly from known theories of choreographies, and in particular introduced the possibility of expressing higher-order choreographies that are fully distributed. In this article, we introduce Chor λ, the first functional choreographic programming language. It is also the first theory that explains the core ideas of higher-order choreographic programming. We show that bridging the gap between practice and theory requires developing a new evaluation strategy and typing discipline for λ terms that accounts for the distributed nature of computation in choreographies.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Graversen, Eva","Lugović, Lovro","Montesi, Fabrizio","Peressotti, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-606176"],"event":{"end":"2022-09-29","place":"Tbilisi, ge","start":"2022-09-27","title":"19th International Colloquium on Theoretical Aspects of Computing, ICTAC 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Graversen, Eva"],"keyword":["Choreographies","Concurrency","Lambda calculus","Type systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"functional choreographic programming","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/215299062/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Work partially supported by Villum Fonden, grant no. 29518."],"id":"S01-000.00-606176","identifier":[{"id":"85140755772","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-732e820d-b317-4aa4-94a4-6def8469de95"],"keyword":["Choreographies","Concurrency","Lambda calculus","Type systems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A28BBCD18522B69F9D1E6F1AD79CA772"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/215299062/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity, and Programming Languages","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"graversenpau","last":"Graversen","locid":"1a2ccb3c-832d-46ea-8d84-6f1e0f0da3dc","name":"Graversen, Eva","orcid":"0000-0002-9430-4907","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lovro","key":"lugovićpau","last":"Lugović","name":"Lugović, Lovro","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"peressottipau","last":"Peressotti","locid":"afca1964-ceda-46fa-b7c7-f6e77e401024","name":"Peressotti, Marco","orcid":"0000-0002-0243-0480","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helmut","key":"seidlpedh","last":"Seidl","name":"Seidl, Helmut","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhiming","key":"liupedh","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Zhiming","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Corina S.","key":"pasareanupedh","last":"Pasareanu","name":"Pasareanu, Corina S.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-17715-6_15","isbn":["9783031177149"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"212-237","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Theoretical Aspects of Computing – ICTAC 2022 - 19th International Colloquium, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140755772"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-732e820d-b317-4aa4-94a4-6def8469de95"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Functional Choreographic Programming","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-606176","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Continuous query answering is a challenging problem faced by systems that need to reason over data as it arrives. Recently, a logic-based approach to this problem has been proposed that advocates generating hypothetical query answers – potential answers that are consistent with the available data, but still require confirmation by future input. The current work studies hypothetical query answering in realistic settings, where data may arrive out of order. This requires revising its semantics and reanalysing the intuitions that led to the design of the existing algorithms, in order to develop a novel incremental online algorithm that takes into account that past data may yet arrive. We also discuss how our methods may be extended to channels with losses.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Gaspar, Graça","Nunes, Isabel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-600797"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-23","place":"Helsinki, fi","start":"2022-06-20","title":"12th International Symposium on Foundations of Information and Knowledge Systems, FoIKS 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lisbon"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can you answer while you wait","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/215299089/paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was partially supported by FCT through the LASIGE Research Unit, ref. UIDB/00408/2020 and ref. UIDP/00408/2020."],"id":"S01-000.00-600797","identifier":[{"id":"85135094034","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-6073bc32-0928-4311-ab96-27a95eaadd23"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C3E5E93BB68158E917B54D961398558C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/215299089/paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity, and Programming Languages","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Graça","key":"gasparpau","last":"Gaspar","name":"Gaspar, Graça","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Isabel","key":"nunespau","last":"Nunes","name":"Nunes, Isabel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ivan","key":"varzinczakpedh","last":"Varzinczak","name":"Varzinczak, Ivan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-11321-5_7","isbn":["9783031113208"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"111-129","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Foundations of Information and Knowledge Systems - 12th International Symposium, FoIKS 2022, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135094034"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6073bc32-0928-4311-ab96-27a95eaadd23"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Can you answer while you wait?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-600797","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The idea of preparing a technical document for the repairs and interventions upon concrete structures goes back to the former fib COM 5: Structural Service Life Aspects, being the goal of the then TG 5.9. After a long period of reduced activity, and taking into account the reorganization of fib commissions that meanwhile took place, on June 2017 a different approach was proposed to push forward the task of TG 8.1 (formerly TG 5.9). The (new) goal of TG 8.1 was to deliver a ‘how-to-do’ guide, gathering together protection, repair, and strengthening techniques for concrete structures. Chapters are intended to provide both guidelines and case-studies, serving as support to the application of fib MC 2020 pre-normative specifications. Each chapter was written by an editorial team comprising desirably at least a researcher, a designer and a contractor. Templates have been prepared in order to harmonize the contents and the presentation of the different methods. Following the writing process, chapters were reviewed by experts and, after amendments by the authors, they underwent a second review process by COM 8 and TG 3.4 members, as well as by different practitioners. For each protection, repair and strengthening method addressed in this guide, readers have a description of when to adopt it, which materials and systems are required, which techniques are available, and what kind of equipment is needed. It then presents a summary of stakeholders’ roles and qualifications, design guidelines referring to most relevant codes and references, the intervention procedure, quality control measures and monitoring and maintenance activities. Due to the extent of the guide, it was decided to publish it as bulletin 102, addressing protection and repair methods, and bulletin 103, addressing strengthening methods. We would like to thank the authors, reviewers and members of COM 8 and TG 3.4 for their work in developing this fib Bulletin, which we hope will be useful for professionals working in the field of existing concrete structures, especially those concerned with life-cycle management and conservation activities. As noted above, this Bulletin is also intended to act as a background and supporting document to the next edition of the fib Model Code for Concrete Structures, which is currently under development under the auspices of TG10.1 with the working title of ‘fib Model Code 2020’. Eduardo Júlio and Eduardo Cavaco","author_count":58,"contributors":["Agnetti, Stefano","Bencardino, Francesco","Buchin-Roulie, Vanessa","Fonseca, Susana Cabral","Chen, Ju","Correia, Luís","Costa, José Paulo","Cynober, Charles","Felice, Gianmarco De","Dourado, Filipe","Dusi, Alberto","Feng, Ran","Guerreiro, Luís","Kunz, Jakob","Laco, Jan","Lima, Luis","Manfredi, Gaetano","Apostolidi, Eftychia","Bilotta, Antonio","Burtscher, Stefan L.","Carvelli, Valter","Chen, Long","Costa, António","Cuzzilla, Roberto","Czaderski-Forchmann, Christoph","Ludovico, Marco Di","Dritsos, Stephanos","Farinha, João","Giarlelis, Christos","Kotynia, Renata","Kyriakides, Nicholas","Lampropoulos, Andreas","Loeffler, Kay","Martinelli, Giorgia","Mateos, Alejandro","Paula, Raquel","Prota, Andrea","Correia, João Ramôa","Repapis, Constantinos","Sandberg, Jessica","Sena-Cruz, José","Su, Meini","Trimboli, Antonio","Vorwagner, Alois","Wang, Zhongwen","Zhang, Dawei","Moseley, Jon","Pinto, Alexandre","Quiertant, Marc","Randl, Norbert","Rousakis, Theodoros","Schmidt, Jacob Wittrup","Shimomura, Takumi","Triantafillou, Thanasis","Ueda, Tamon","Wang, Shengnian","Xing, Feng","Zhu, Ji-Hua"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-120001"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Argentina","Austria","China","Cyprus","France","Germany","Greece","Italy","Japan","Liechtenstein","Poland","Portugal","Slovakia","Switzerland","United Kingdom","U