{"abstract":"Choreographies are formal descriptions of distributed systems, which focus on the way in which participants communicate. While they are useful for analysing protocols, in practice systems are written directly by specifying each participant’s behaviour. This created the need for choreography extraction: the process of obtaining a choreography that faithfully describes the collective behaviour of all participants in a distributed protocol. Previous works have addressed this problem for systems with a predefined, finite number of participants. In this work, we show how to extract choreographies from system descriptions where the total number of participants is unknown and unbounded, due to the ability of spawning new processes at runtime. This extension is challenging, since previous algorithms relied heavily on the set of possible states of the network during execution being finite.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kjær, Bjørn Angel","Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Montesi, Fabrizio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-575957"],"event":{"end":"2022-09-23","place":"Tbilisi, ge","start":"2022-09-21","title":"32nd International Symposium on Logic-Based Program Synthesis and Transformation, LOPSTR 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"keyword":["Choreography","Concurrency","Extraction","Message passing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from infinity to choreographies extraction for unbounded systems","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/215299144/ExtendingExtraction.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Partially supported by Villum Fonden, grant no. 29518."],"id":"S01-000.00-575957","identifier":[{"id":"85138775151","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-09ae649d-2cfe-4dbf-8ef3-94e7cda70b29"],"keyword":["Choreography","Concurrency","Extraction","Message passing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BC890430E74B8FD65C72932C4EF2D5D9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/215299144/ExtendingExtraction.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjørn Angel","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","name":"Kjær, Bjørn Angel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Alicia","key":"villanuevapedh","last":"Villanueva","name":"Villanueva, Alicia","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-16767-6_6","isbn":["9783031167669"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"103-120","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"32nd International Symposium, LOPSTR 2022, Proceedings","title":"Logic-Based Program Synthesis and Transformation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138775151"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-09ae649d-2cfe-4dbf-8ef3-94e7cda70b29"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"From infinity to choreographies : Extraction for unbounded Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-575957","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Hypothetical continuous query answering over data streams was introduced as a way to anticipate answers to queries that depend on facts that may or may not happen in the future. Previous work has studied this problem for Temporal Datalog with negation and instantaneous communication, showing that hypothetical answers can be incrementally updated as new data arrives at the data stream. In practice, individual communications take variable amounts of time, so data may arrive delayed and unordered. This motivates studying hypothetical continuous query answering in a setting with communication delays. The interaction between communication delays and negation is however problematic, and the existing approach is restricted to the positive fragment of the language. In this work we show how to remove this restriction by defining an appropriate operational semantics based on fixpoint theory, and showing that the relevant fixpoints can be computed in finite time by a carefully designed algorithm.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Gaspar, Graça","Nunes, Isabel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-611647"],"event":{"end":"2022-09-29","place":"Tbilisi, ge","start":"2022-09-27","title":"19th International Colloquium on Theoretical Aspects of Computing, ICTAC 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lisbon"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reconciling communication delays and negation","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/215298990/paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Partially supported by FCT through the LASIGE Research Unit, ref. UIDB/00408/ 2020 and ref. UIDP/00408/2020."],"id":"S01-000.00-611647","identifier":[{"id":"85140770658","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-862901b5-90b2-485f-8a85-34e3d00eee76"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2D81C4438EF675279160D56CEA7AF5EB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/215298990/paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity, and Programming Languages","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Graça","key":"gasparpau","last":"Gaspar","name":"Gaspar, Graça","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Isabel","key":"nunespau","last":"Nunes","name":"Nunes, Isabel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helmut","key":"seidlpedh","last":"Seidl","name":"Seidl, Helmut","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhiming","key":"liupedh","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Zhiming","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Corina S.","key":"pasareanupedh","last":"Pasareanu","name":"Pasareanu, Corina S.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-17715-6_11","isbn":["9783031177149"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"151-169","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Theoretical Aspects of Computing – ICTAC 2022 - 19th International Colloquium, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140770658"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-862901b5-90b2-485f-8a85-34e3d00eee76"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Reconciling Communication Delays and Negation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-611647","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Choreographic programming is a paradigm for developing concurrent and distributed systems, where programs are choreographies that define, from a global viewpoint, the computations and interactions that communicating processes should enact. Choreography compilation translates choreographies into the local definitions of process behaviours, given as terms in a process calculus. Proving choreography compilation correct is challenging and error-prone, because it requires relating languages in different paradigms (global interactions vs local actions) and dealing with a combinatorial explosion of proof cases. We present the first certified program for choreography compilation for a nontrivial choreographic language supporting recursion.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Montesi, Fabrizio","Peressotti, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-631825"],"event":{"end":"2021-09-10","place":"Virtual, Online","start":"2021-09-08","title":"18th International Colloquium on Theoretical Aspects of Computing, ICTAC 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"keyword":["Choreographic Programming","Compilation","Formalisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"certifying choreography compilation","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2102.10698","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-631825","identifier":[{"id":"85115182661","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-cc9a18dc-4131-4e35-80ff-a2c758573baf"],"keyword":["Choreographic programming","Compilation","Formalisation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D860FC21C56370E82CB7965B7D617AE6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2102.10698","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity, and Programming Languages","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"peressottipau","last":"Peressotti","locid":"afca1964-ceda-46fa-b7c7-f6e77e401024","name":"Peressotti, Marco","orcid":"0000-0002-0243-0480","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Antonio","key":"ceronepedh","last":"Cerone","name":"Cerone, Antonio","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter Csaba","key":"olveczkypedh","last":"Olveczky","name":"Olveczky, Peter Csaba","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-85315-0_8","isbn":["9783030853143"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"115-133","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"18th International Colloquium","title":"Theoretical Aspects of Computing – ICTAC 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115182661"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-cc9a18dc-4131-4e35-80ff-a2c758573baf"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Certifying Choreography Compilation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-631825","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Approximation fixpoint theory (AFT) is an algebraic study of fixpoints of lattice operators that unifies various knowledge representation formalisms. In AFT, stratification of operators has been studied, essentially resulting in a theory that specifies when certain types of fixpoints can be computed stratum per stratum. Recently, novel types of fixpoints related to groundedness have been introduced in AFT. In this article, we study how those fixpoints behave under stratified operators. One recent application domain of AFT is the field of active integrity constraints (AICs). We apply our extended stratification theory to AICs and find that existing notions of stratification in AICs are covered by this general algebraic definition of stratification. As a result, we obtain stratification results for a large variety of semantics for AICs.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Bogaerts, Bart","Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-582022"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bogaerts, Bart"],"country":["Belgium"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Free University of Brussels"],"keyword":["Active integrity constraints","Semantics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stratification in approximation fixpoint theory and its application to active integrity constraints","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/180002764/AIC_Stratification.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-582022","identifier":[{"id":"85100092830","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-1ec31542-84e8-4649-8556-8296f7d0e3fc"],"keyword":["Active integrity constraints","fixpoints","semantics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-66347BF0ADC7C12391DF213B5E23FD53"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/180002764/AIC_Stratification.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"be","key":"free university of brussels","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Free University of Brussels","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bart","key":"bogaertspau","last":"Bogaerts","name":"Bogaerts, Bart","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3430750","issn":["15293785","1557945X"],"issn_org":["15293785"],"issue":"1","journal":"ACM Transactions on Computational Logic","paperid":"6","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Transactions on Computational Logic","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100092830"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1ec31542-84e8-4649-8556-8296f7d0e3fc"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Stratification in Approximation Fixpoint Theory and Its Application to Active Integrity Constraints","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-582022","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The theory of choreographic languages typically includes a number of complex results that are proved by structural induction. The high number of cases and the subtle details in some of them lead to long reviewing processes, and occasionally to errors being found in published proofs. In this work, we take a published proof of Turing completeness of a choreographic language and formalise it in Coq. Our development includes formalising the choreographic language, its basic properties, Kleene's theory of partial recursive functions, the encoding of these functions as choreographies, and a proof that this encoding is correct. With this effort, we show that theorem proving can be a very useful tool in the field of choreographic languages: besides the added degree of confidence that we get from a mechanised proof, the formalisation process led us to a significant simplification of the underlying theory. Our results offer a foundation for the future formal development of choreographic languages.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Montesi, Fabrizio","Peressotti, Marco"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-643731"],"event":{"acronym":"ECOOP","end":"2021-07-01","place":"Virtual, Rome, it","start":"2021-06-29","title":"12th International Conference on Interactive Theorem Proving, ITP 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"keyword":["Choreographic Programming","Formalisation","Turing completeness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formalising a turing complete choreographic language in coq","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ITP.2021.15","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Work partially supported by Villum Fonden, grant no. 29518."],"id":"S01-000.00-643731","identifier":[{"id":"85114810608","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-f67b2020-af4d-4227-9b72-dc32a7445a83"],"keyword":["Choreographic Programming","Formalisation","Turing Completeness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8928A3E970D5E54B5F878BCE11BFF994"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.ITP.2021.15","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/184459948/LIPIcs_ITP_2021_15.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Cybersecurity, and Programming Languages","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luis","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","name_org":"Cruz-Filipe, Luis","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":