{"abstract":"Choreographic Programming is a paradigm for developing concurrent programs that are deadlock-free by construction, as a result of programming communications declaratively and then synthesising process implementations automatically. Despite strong interest on choreographies, a foundational model that explains which computations can be performed with the hallmark constructs of choreographies is still missing. In this work, we introduce Core Choreographies (CC), a model that includes only the core primitives of choreographic programming. Every computable function can be implemented as a choreography in CC, from which we can synthesise a process implementation where independent computations run in parallel. We discuss the design of CC and argue that it constitutes a canonical model for choreographic programming.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Montesi, Fabrizio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-587753"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"keyword":["Choreography","Computability","Process calculi"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a core model for choreographic programming","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1510.03271.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank Hugo Torres Vieira and Gianluigi Zavattaro for their useful comments. Montesi was supported by CRC (Choreographies for Reliable and efficient Communication software), grant No. DFF–4005-00304 from the Danish Council for Independent Research . Appendix A"],"id":"S01-000.00-587753","identifier":[{"id":"85068847215","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-32c20848-687c-4c01-a012-cf78ea15d538"],"keyword":["Choreography","Computability","Process calculi"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7A610D5A7130DEB8A9F1FD53BA987B2E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1510.03271.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.tcs.2019.07.005","issn":["03043975"],"journal":"Theoretical Computer Science","pages":"38-66","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Theoretical Computer Science","volume":"802"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85068847215"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-32c20848-687c-4c01-a012-cf78ea15d538"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A core model for choreographic programming","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-587753","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Continuous queries over data streams often delay answers until some relevant input arrives through the data stream. These delays may turn answers, when they arrive, obsolete to users who sometimes have to make decisions with no help whatsoever. Therefore, it can be useful to provide hypothetical answers – “given the current information, it is possible that X will become true at time t” – instead of no information at all. In this paper we present a semantics for queries and corresponding answers that covers such hypothetical answers, together with an online algorithm for updating the set of facts that are consistent with the currently available information.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Gaspar, Graça","Nunes, Isabel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-589312"],"event":{"end":"2020-02-12","place":"New York, us","start":"2020-02-07","title":"34th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence, AAAI 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lisbon"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hypothetical answers to continuous queries over data streams","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85106410962","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Acknowledgements. This work was partially supported by the Independent Research Fund Denmark, grant DFF-7014-00041, and by UID/MULTI/04046/2019 Research Unit grant from FCT, Portugal (to BioISI)."],"id":"S01-000.00-589312","identifier":[{"id":"85106410962","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-385d10b3-4bbd-4a13-8428-bb1299617ccf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-1C5254B40E9E3A9741C24EF90576DC08"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Graça","key":"gasparpau","last":"Gaspar","name":"Gaspar, Graça","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Isabel","key":"nunespau","last":"Nunes","name":"Nunes, Isabel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781577358350"],"pages":"2798-2805","publisher":"AAAI Press","status":"p","title":"AAAI 2020 - 34th AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106410962"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-385d10b3-4bbd-4a13-8428-bb1299617ccf"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Hypothetical answers to continuous queries over data streams","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-589312","year":"2020","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The Boolean Pythagorean Triples problem asks: does there exist a binary coloring of the natural numbers such that every Pythagorean triple contains an element of each color? This problem was first solved in 2016, when Heule, Kullmann and Marek encoded a finite restriction of this problem as a propositional formula and showed its unsatisfiability. In this work we formalize their development in the theorem prover Coq. We state the Boolean Pythagorean Triples problem in Coq, define its encoding as a propositional formula and establish the relation between solutions to the problem and satisfying assignments to the formula. We verify Heule et al.’s proof by showing that the symmetry breaks they introduced to simplify the propositional formula are sound, and by implementing a correct-by-construction checker for proofs of unsatisfiability based on reverse unit propagation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Marques-Silva, Joao","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-602176"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lisbon"],"keyword":["Interactive theorem proving","Large scale proofs","SAT solving"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formally verifying the solution to the boolean pythagorean triples problem","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85055893611","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-602176","identifier":[{"id":"85055893611","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-65480451-893c-46ab-8200-1c64b1fc711c"],"keyword":["Interactive theorem proving","Large-scale proofs","SAT solving"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-957EDA5495ACF9CD789E5F7FB68892D2"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joao","key":"marquessilvapau","last":"Marques-Silva","name":"Marques-Silva, Joao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10817-018-9490-4","issn":["01687433","15730670"],"issn_org":["01687433"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Automated Reasoning","pages":"695-722","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Automated Reasoning","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055893611"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-65480451-893c-46ab-8200-1c64b1fc711c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Formally Verifying the Solution to the Boolean Pythagorean Triples Problem","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-602176","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
