epartment of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ar","key":"university of buenos aires","loc":["Argentina","America, South"],"name":"University of Buenos Aires","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Massimo","key":"bartolettipau","last":"Bartoletti","name":"Bartoletti, Massimo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maurice H.","key":"terbeekpau","last":"Ter Beek","name":"Ter Beek, Maurice H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Hernán","key":"melgrattipau","last":"Melgratti","name":"Melgratti, Hernán","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781450344869"],"pages":"1309-1311","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Symposium on Applied Computing"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b72bb058-8c65-4216-97f6-c32ce70aaff7"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Editorial message: Special Track on Service-Oriented Architectures and Programming (SOAP)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-625718","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Recent successes in formally verifying increasingly larger computer-generated proofs have relied extensively on (a) using oracles, to find answers for recurring subproblems efficiently, and (b) extracting formally verified checkers, to perform exhaustive case analysis in feasible time. In this work we present a formal verification of optimality of sorting networks on up to 9 inputs, making it one of the largest computer-generated proofs that has been formally verified. We show that an adequate pre-processing of the information provided by the oracle is essential for feasibility, as it improves the time required by our extracted checker by several orders of magnitude.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Larsen, Kim Skak","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-629540"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Interactive theorem proving","Large scale proofs","Sorting networks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formally proving size optimality of sorting networks","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85011266645","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-629540","identifier":[{"id":"85011266645","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-c499aa7f-a152-4ac2-9781-b62202884c89"],"keyword":["Interactive theorem proving","Large-scale proofs","Program extraction","Sorting networks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F8482CF3AB8187C6CC4CC230E523962F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luis","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","name_org":"Cruz-Filipe, Luis","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim S.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"0ecf13aa-3ad6-43a2-bd87-35fe8761ac7a","name":"Larsen, Kim Skak","name_org":"Larsen, Kim S.","orcid":"0000-0003-0560-3794","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10817-017-9405-9","issn":["01687433","15730670"],"issn_org":["01687433"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Automated Reasoning","pages":"425-454","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Automated Reasoning","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85011266645"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c499aa7f-a152-4ac2-9781-b62202884c89"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Formally Proving Size Optimality of Sorting Networks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-629540","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Formal verification of large computer-generated proofs often relies on certified checkers based on oracles. We propose a methodology for such proofs, advocating a separation of concerns between formalizing the underlying theory and optimizing the algorithm implemented in the checker, based on the observation that such optimizations can benefit significantly from adequately adapting the oracle.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Larsen, Kim Skak","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-583487"],"event":{"acronym":"ITP","end":"2017-09-29","place":"Brasília, br","start":"2017-09-26","title":"8th International Conference on Interactive Theorem Proving","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how to get more out of your oracles","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85029502346","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-583487","identifier":[{"id":"85029502346","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-23f0447b-c67e-46cf-9e8d-5619d48c49b6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F1F36524F33EA3585C3EACE3E84C3044"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Skak","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"0ecf13aa-3ad6-43a2-bd87-35fe8761ac7a","name":"Larsen, Kim Skak","orcid":"0000-0003-0560-3794","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mauricio","key":"ayalarincónpedh","last":"Ayala-Rincón","name":"Ayala-Rincón, Mauricio","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"César A.","key":"muñozpedh","last":"Muñoz","name":"Muñoz, César A.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-66107-0_11","eisbn":["9783319661070"],"isbn":["9783319661063"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"164-170","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 8th International Conference on Interactive Theorem Proving"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029502346"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-23f0447b-c67e-46cf-9e8d-5619d48c49b6"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"How to Get More Out of Your Oracles","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-583487","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We present a novel propositional proof tracing format that eliminates complex processing, thus enabling efficient (formal) proof checking. The benefits of this format are demonstrated by implementing a proof checker in C, which outperforms a state-of-the-art checker by two orders of magnitude. We then formalize the theory underlying propositional proof checking in Coq, and extract a correct-by-construction proof checker for our format from the formalization. An empirical evaluation using 280 unsatisfiable instances from the 2015 and 2016 SAT competitions shows that this certified checker usually performs comparably to a state-of-the-art non-certified proof checker. Using this format, we formally verify the recent 200 TB proof of the Boolean Pythagorean Triples conjecture.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Marques-Silva, Joao","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-610052"],"event":{"acronym":"TACAS","end":"2017-04-29","place":"Uppsala, se","start":"2017-04-22","title":"23rd International Conference on Tools and Algorithms for the Construction and Analysis of Systems","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lisbon"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficient certified resolution proof checking","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/141252008/Efficient_Certified_Resolution_Proof_Checking.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-610052","identifier":[{"id":"85017507708","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-80cad6ac-1740-458e-ab0c-0012ad3a6db5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-691558E1C90A4D6BC36D6C63F55AA590"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/141252008/Efficient_Certified_Resolution_Proof_Checking.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1610.06984.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joao","key":"marquessilvapau","last":"Marques-Silva","name":"Marques-Silva, Joao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Tiziana","key":"margariapedh","last":"Margaria","name":"Margaria, Tiziana","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Axel","key":"legaypedh","last":"Legay","name":"Legay, Axel","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-54577-5_7","eisbn":["9783662545775"],"isbn":["9783662545768"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"118-135","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 3rd International Conference, TACAS 2017, Held as Part of the European Joint Conferences on Theory and Practice of Software, ETAPS 2017, Uppsala, Sweden, April 22-29, 2017","title":"Tools and Algorithms for the Construction and Analysis of Systems","volume":"Part I"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017507708"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-80cad6ac-1740-458e-ab0c-0012ad3a6db5"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Efficient Certified Resolution Proof Checking","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-610052","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Choreographic Programming is an emerging paradigm for correct-by-construction concurrent programming. However, its applicability is limited by the current lack of support for reusable procedures. We propose Procedural Choreographies (PC), a choreographic language model with full procedural abstraction. PC includes unbounded process creation and name mobility, yielding a powerful framework for writing correct concurrent algorithms that can be compiled into a process calculus. This increased expressivity requires a typing discipline to ensure that processes are properly connected when enacting procedures.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Montesi, Fabrizio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-614062"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-22","place":"Neuchatel, ch","start":"2017-06-19","title":"37th IFIP WG 6.1 International Conference on Formal Techniques for Distributed Objects, Components, and Systems, FORTE 2017 - Held as Part of the 12th International Federated Conference on Distributed Computing Techniques, DisCoTec 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"procedural choreographic programming","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/141251779/Procedural_Choreographic_Programming.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-614062","identifier":[{"id":"85020515248","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-8e8d3b0c-06fe-43a9-b5c6-7beefa0f4ca3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-92CE409B822E84D7652E6C810AD9C6F4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/141251779/Procedural_Choreographic_Programming.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1602.03729.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luis","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","name_org":"Cruz-Filipe, Luis","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ahmed","key":"bouajjanipedh","last":"Bouajjani","name":"Bouajjani, Ahmed","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alexandra","key":"silvapedh","last":"Silva","name":"Silva, Alexandra","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-60225-7_7","eisbn":["9783319602257"],"isbn":["9783319602240"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"92-107","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"37th IFIP WG 6.1 International Conference, FORTE 2017, Held as Part of the 12th International Federated Conference on Distributed Computing Techniques, DisCoTec 2017, Neuchâtel, Switzerland, June 19-22, 2017","title":"Formal Techniques for Distributed Objects, Components, and Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020515248"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8e8d3b0c-06fe-43a9-b5c6-7beefa0f4ca3"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Procedural Choreographic Programming","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-614062","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Choreographic Programming is a paradigm for developing concurrent programs that are deadlock-free by construction, by programming communications declaratively and then synthesising process implementations automatically. Despite strong interest on choreographies, a foundational model that explains which computations can be performed with the hallmark constructs of choreographies is still missing. In this work, we introduce Core Choreographies (CC), a model that includes only the core primitives of choreographic programming. Every computable function can be implemented as a choreography in CC, from which we can synthesise a process implementation where independent computations run in parallel. We discuss the design of CC and argue that it constitutes a canonical model for choreographic programming.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Montesi, Fabrizio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-620480"],"event":{"end":"2016-10-21","place":"Besançon, fr","start":"2016-10-19","title":"13th International Formal Aspects of Component Software Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a core model for choreographic programming","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/141250624/A_Core_Model_for_Choreographic_Programming.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-620480","identifier":[{"id":"85018363984","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-a5247593-c6fa-4997-917e-30ab2ec8f424"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C4884B47F34D29234330B1FA153AD9DE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https: