of Component Software"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018363984"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-a5247593-c6fa-4997-917e-30ab2ec8f424"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A Core Model for Choreographic Programming","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-620480","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In 2016, Heule, Kullmann and Marek solved the Boolean Pythagorean Triples problem: is there a binary coloring of the natural numbers such that every Pythagorean triple contains an element of each color? By encoding a finite portion of this problem as a propositional formula and showing its unsatisfiability, they established that such a coloring does not exist. Subsequently, this answer was verified by a correct-by-construction checker extracted from a Coq formalization, which was able to reproduce the original proof. However, none of these works address the question of formally addressing the relationship between the propositional formula that was constructed and the mathematical problem being considered. In this work, we formalize the Boolean Pythagorean Triples problem in Coq. We recursively define a family of propositional formulas, parameterized on a natural number n, and show that unsatisfiability of this formula for any particular n implies that there does not exist a solution to the problem. We then formalize the mathematical argument behind the simplification step in the original proof of unsatisfiability and the logical argument underlying cube-and-conquer, obtaining a verified proof of Heule et al.’s solution.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-638809"],"event":{"acronym":"LPAR","end":"2017-05-12","place":"Maun, bw","start":"2017-05-07","title":"21st International Conference on Logic for Programming, Artificial Intelligence and Reasoning","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formally proving the boolean triples conjecture","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.29007/jvdj","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-638809","ids":["sdu-e51a8ddd-9752-469b-8270-a08eb90cc8dc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-29656E0D7AECF219135D8AB065E208D8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/146531374/Formally_Proving_the_Boolean_Triples_Conjecture.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.29007/jvdj","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luis","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","name_org":"Cruz-Filipe, Luis","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"eiterpedh","last":"Eiter","name":"Eiter, Thomas","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"sandspedh","last":"Sands","name":"Sands, David","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.29007/jvdj","issn":["23987340"],"pages":"509-522","publisher":"EasyChair Publications","series":"EPiC Series in Computing","status":"p","subtitle":"21st International Conference on Logic for Programming, Artificial Intelligence and Reasoning","title":"Proceedings of LPAR-21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e51a8ddd-9752-469b-8270-a08eb90cc8dc"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Formally Proving the Boolean Triples Conjecture","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-638809","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We introduce a formalism to couple integrity constraints over general-purpose knowledge bases with actions that can be executed to restore consistency. This formalism generalizes active integrity constraints over databases. In the more general setting of multi-context systems, adding repair suggestions to integrity constraints allows defining simple iterative algorithms to find all possible grounded repairs – repairs for the global system that follow the suggestions given by the actions in the individual rules. We apply our methodology to ontologies, and show that it can express most relevant types of integrity constraints in this domain.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Gaspar, Graça","Nunes, Isabel","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-630849"],"event":{"end":"2016-11-23","place":"Bologna, it","start":"2016-11-19","title":"20th International Conference on Knowledge Engineering and Knowledge Management","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lisbon"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"active integrity constraints for multi context systems","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1609.06019.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-630849","identifier":[{"id":"84997503327","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-c922eecd-0e43-4fbf-bf5d-43206439e391"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2E165FB5BBF8932B6CF48A10F679978A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1609.06019.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Graça","key":"gasparpau","last":"Gaspar","name":"Gaspar, Graça","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Isabel","key":"nunespau","last":"Nunes","name":"Nunes, Isabel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eva","key":"blomqvistpedh","last":"Blomqvist","name":"Blomqvist, Eva","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Paolo","key":"ciancarinipedh","last":"Ciancarini","name":"Ciancarini, Paolo","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Francesco","key":"poggipedh","last":"Poggi","name":"Poggi, Francesco","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Fabio","key":"vitalipedh","last":"Vitali","name":"Vitali, Fabio","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-49004-5_7","eisbn":["9783319490045"],"isbn":["9783319490038"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"98-112","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"20th International Conference, EKAW 2016, Bologna, Italy, November 19-23, 2016, Proceedings","title":"Knowledge Engineering and Knowledge Management"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84997503327"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c922eecd-0e43-4fbf-bf5d-43206439e391"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Active Integrity Constraints for Multi-context Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-630849","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The formalism of active integrity constraints was introduced as a way to specify particular classes of integrity constraints over relational databases together with preferences on how to repair existing inconsistencies. The rule-based syntax of such integrity constraints also provides algorithms for finding such repairs that achieve the best asymptotic complexity. However, the different semantics that have been proposed for these integrity constraints all exhibit some counter-intuitive examples. In this work, we look at active integrity constraints using ideas from algebraic fixpoint theory. We show how database repairs can be modeled as fixpoints of particular operators on databases, and study how the notion of grounded fixpoint induces a corresponding notion of grounded database repair that captures several natural intuitions, and in particular avoids the problems of previous alternative semantics. In order to study grounded repairs in their full generality, we need to generalize the notion of grounded fixpoint to non-deterministic operators. We propose such a definition and illustrate its plausibility in the database context.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-583926"],"event":{"acronym":"ICLP","end":"2016-10-21","place":"New York, us","start":"2016-10-16","title":"32nd International Conference on Logic Programming","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Active integrity constraints"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"grounded fixpoints and active integrity constraints","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/OASIcs.ICLP.2016.11","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-583926","identifier":[{"id":"85004007050","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-25464bdb-9603-4a47-b552-0506f54ab03b"],"keyword":["Active integrity constraints","Grounded fixpoints"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-1964B94C23306854C23AFDBBCD519DAD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/OASIcs.ICLP.2016.11","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/123229909/Grounded_Fixpoints_and_Active_Integrity_Constraints.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Manuel","key":"carropedh","last":"Carro","name":"Carro, Manuel","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Andy","key":"kingpedh","last":"King","name":"King, Andy","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Neda","key":"saeedloeipedh","last":"Saeedloei","name":"Saeedloei, Neda","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Marina","key":"devospedh","last":"De Vos","name":"De Vos, Marina","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/oasics.iclp.2016.11","isbn":["9783959770071"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl-Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","status":"p","title":"Technical Communications of the 32nd International Conference on Logic Programming"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85004007050"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-25464bdb-9603-4a47-b552-0506f54ab03b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Grounded Fixpoints and Active Integrity Constraints","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-583926","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Integrity constraints in databases have been studied extensively since the 1980s, and they are considered essential to guarantee database integrity. In recent years, several authors have studied how the same notion can be adapted to reasoning frameworks, in such a way that they achieve the purpose of guaranteeing a system’s consistency, but are kept separate from the reasoning mechanisms. In this paper we focus on multi-context systems, a general-purpose framework for combining heterogeneous reasoning systems, enhancing them with a notion of integrity constraints that generalizes the corresponding concept in the database world.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Nunes, Isabel","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-634632"],"event":{"acronym":"FoIKS","end":"2016-03-11","place":"Linz, at","start":"2016-03-07","title":"9th International Symposium on Foundations of Information and Knowledge Systems","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lisbon"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integrity constraints for general purpose knowledge bases","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84960355219","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-634632","identifier":[{"id":"84960355219","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-d6698980-8ab8-4a61-9aa9-7611bce6ead0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C0EBA3ED20D19A47F745BD67877EB458"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pt","key":"university of lisbon","loc":["Portugal","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lisbon","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luis","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","name_org":"Cruz-Filipe, Luis","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Isabel","key":"nunespau","last":"Nunes","name":"Nunes, Isabel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marc","key":"gyssenspedh","last":"Gyssens","name":"Gyssens, Marc","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Guillermo","key":"simaripedh","last":"Simari","name":"Simari, Guillermo","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-30024-5_13","eisbn":["9783319300245"],"isbn":["9783319300238"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"235-254","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 9th International Symposium on Foundations of Information and Knowledge Systems","title":"FoIKS 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960355219"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-d6698980-8ab8-4a61-9aa9-7611bce6ead0"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Integrity Constraints for General-Purpose Knowledge Bases","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-634632","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes a computer-assisted non-existence proof of 9-input sorting networks consisting of 24 comparators, hence showing that the 25-comparator sorting network found by Floyd in 1964 is optimal. As a corollary, the 29-comparator network found by Waksman in 1969 is optimal when sorting 10 inputs. This closes the two smallest open instances of the optimal-size sorting network problem, which have been open since the results of Floyd and Knuth from 1966 proving optimality for sorting networks of up to 8 inputs.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Codish, Michael","Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Frank, Michael","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-590353"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ben-Gurion University of the Negev"],"keyword":["Symmetry breaking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sorting nine inputs requires twenty five comparisons","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84950264544","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-590353","identifier":[{"id":"84950264544","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-3bc81d51-96fd-4f09-b22b-7d095b02e650"],"keyword":["Symmetry breaking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4734372F2C59D23AE70C1142CE75C270"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"il","key":"ben gurion university of the negev","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Ben-Gurion University of the Negev","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"codishpau","last":"Codish","name":"Codish, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luis","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","name_org":"Cruz-Filipe, Luis","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"frankpau","last":"Frank","name":"Frank, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcss.2015.11.014","issn":["00220000","10902724"],"issn_org":["00220000"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Computer and System Sciences","pages":"551-563","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Computer and System Sciences","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84950264544"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3bc81d51-96fd-4f09-b22b-7d095b02e650"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Sorting nine inputs requires twenty-five comparisons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-590353","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Choreographic Programming is a development methodology for concurrent software that guarantees correctness by construction. The key to this paradigm is to disallow mismatched I/O operations in programs, and mechanically synthesise process implementations. There is still a lack of practical illustrations of the applicability of choreographies to computational problems with standard concurrent solutions. In this work, we explore the potential of choreographic programming by writing concurrent algorithms for sorting, solving linear equations, and computing Fast Fourier Transforms. The lessons learned from this experiment give directions for future improvements of the paradigm.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Montesi, Fabrizio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-621533"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-09","place":"Heraklion, gr","start":"2016-06-06","title":"FORTE - The 36th IFIP International Conference on Formal Techniques for Distributed Objects, Components and Systems","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"choreographies in practice","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1602.08863.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-621533","identifier":[{"id":"84977546519","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-a8c94f76-c211-4897-a22f-8c5c1b784d7c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-015E3DD2C48F387C47DF6930C87CB03D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1602.08863.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elvira","key":"albertpedh","last":"Albert","name":"Albert, Elvira","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Ivan","key":"lanesepedh","last":"Lanese","name":"Lanese, Ivan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-39570-8_8","eisbn":["9783319395708"],"isbn":["9783319395692"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"114-123","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"36th IFIP WG 6.1 International Conference, FORTE 2016, Held as Part of the 11th International Federated Conference on Distributed Computing Techniques, DisCoTec 2016, Heraklion, Crete, Greece, June 6-9, 2016, Proceedings","title":"Formal Techniques for Distributed Objects, Components, and Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84977546519"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-a8c94f76-c211-4897-a22f-8c5c1b784d7c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Choreographies in Practice","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-621533","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This paper studies properties of the back end of a sorting network and illustrates the utility of these in the search for networks of optimal size or depth. All previous works focus on properties of the front end of networks and on how to apply these to break symmetries in the search. The new properties help shed understanding on how sorting networks sort and speed-up solvers for both optimal size and depth by an order of magnitude.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Codish, Michael","Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-627242"],"event":{"acronym":"LATA","end":"2015-03-06","place":"Nice, fr","start":"2015-03-02","title":"9th International Conference on Language and Automata Theory and Applications","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ben-Gurion University of the Negev"],"keyword":["SAT solving","Sorting networks","Symmetry breaking"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sorting networks the end game","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-15579-1_52","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-627242","identifier":[{"id":"84928822616","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-bc7b9d71-b927-48fc-8d9a-f22d931aaf08"],"keyword":["SAT solving","Sorting networks","Symmetry breaking"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3ACDB6C70E23BE40C47FC8643408FE2D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-15579-1_52","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"il","key":"ben gurion university of the negev","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Ben-Gurion University of the Negev","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"codishpau","last":"Codish","name":"Codish, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Adrian-Horia","key":"dediupedh","last":"Dediu","name":"Dediu, Adrian-Horia","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Carlos","key":"martínvidepedh","last":"Martín-Vide","name":"Martín-Vide, Carlos","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Enrico","key":"formentipedh","last":"Formenti","name":"Formenti, Enrico","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Bianca","key":"truthepedh","last":"Truthe","name":"Truthe, Bianca","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-15579-1_52","eisbn":["9783319155791"],"isbn":["9783319155784"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"664-675","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th International Conference on Language and Automata Theory and Applications (LATA 2015)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84928822616"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-bc7b9d71-b927-48fc-8d9a-f22d931aaf08"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Sorting Networks: The End Game","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-627242","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Originally proposed in the mid-90s, design patterns for software development played a key role in object-oriented programming not only in increasing software quality, but also by giving a better understanding of the power and limitations of this paradigm. Since then, several authors have endorsed a similar task for other programming paradigms, in the hope of achieving similar benefits. In this paper we present a set of design patterns for Mdl-programs, a hybrid formalism combining several description logic knowledge bases via a logic program. These patterns are extensively applied in a natural way in a large-scale example that illustrates how their usage greatly simplifies some programming tasks, at the level of both development and extension. We also discuss some limitations of this formalism, examining some usual patterns in other programming paradigms that have no parallel in Mdl-programs.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Gaspar, Graca","Nunes, Isabel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-642352"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design patterns for description logic programs","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84942636654","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-642352","identifier":[{"id":"84942636654","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-f188acab-0c26-407e-8c24-4a1530cefa5d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F107EE4256F420A7210C1DE2326E2C99"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luis","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","name_org":"Cruz-Filipe, Luis","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Graca","key":"gasparpau","last":"Gaspar","name":"Gaspar, Graca","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Isabel","key":"nunespau","last":"Nunes","name":"Nunes, Isabel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ana","key":"fredpedh","last":"Fred","name":"Fred, Ana","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan L.G.","key":"dietzpedh","last":"Dietz","name":"Dietz, Jan L.G.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kecheng.","key":"liupedh","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Kecheng.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Joaquim","key":"filipepedh","last":"Filipe","name":"Filipe, Joaquim","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-46549-3_13","eisbn":["9783662465493"],"isbn":["9783662465486"],"issn":["18650929"],"pages":"199-214","publisher":"Springer","series":"Communications in Computer and Information Science","status":"p","subtitle":"5th International Joint Conference, IC3K 2013, Vilamoura, Portugal, September 19-22, 2013. Revised Selected Papers","title":"Knowledge Discovery, Knowledge Engineering and Knowledge Management"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84942636654"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-f188acab-0c26-407e-8c24-4a1530cefa5d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Design Patterns for Description-logic Programs","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-642352","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"In recent work, we formalized the theory of optimal-size sorting networks with the goal of extracting a verified checker for the large-scale computer-generated proof that 25 comparisons are optimal when sorting 9 inputs, which required more than a decade of CPU time and produced 27 GB of proof witnesses. The checker uses an untrusted oracle based on these witnesses and is able to verify the smaller case of 8 inputs within a couple of days, but it did not scale to the full proof for 9 inputs. In this paper, we describe several non-trivial optimizations of the algorithm in the checker, obtained by appropriately changing the formalization and capitalizing on the symbiosis with an adequate implementation of the oracle. We provide experimental evidence of orders of magnitude improvements to both runtime and memory footprint for 8 inputs, and actually manage to check the full proof for 9 inputs.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-579755"],"event":{"end":"2015-07-17","place":"Washington, us","start":"2015-07-13","title":"8th International Conference on Intelligent Computer Mathematics","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimizing a certified proof checker for a large scale computer generated proof","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-20615-8_4","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-579755","identifier":[{"id":"84949967624","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-16ee8c23-ebf1-482e-9526-3b40862c464e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-70BA7907481347DF405C704E93DCEACB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-20615-8_4","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Manfred","key":"kerberpedh","last":"Kerber","name":"Kerber, Manfred","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacques","key":"carettepedh","last":"Carette","name":"Carette, Jacques","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cezary","key":"kaliszykpedh","last":"Kaliszyk","name":"Kaliszyk, Cezary","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Florian","key":"rabepedh","last":"Rabe","name":"Rabe, Florian","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Volker","key":"sorgepedh","last":"Sorge","name":"Sorge, Volker","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-20615-8_4","eisbn":["9783319206158"],"isbn":["9783319206141"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"55-70","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 8th Conference on Intelligent Computer Mathematics (CICM 2015)","title":"Intelligent Computer Mathematics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84949967624"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-16ee8c23-ebf1-482e-9526-3b40862c464e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Optimizing a Certified Proof Checker for a Large-Scale Computer-Generated Proof","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-579755","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents an application of the theory of sorting networks to facilitate the synthesis of optimized general-purpose sorting libraries. Standard sorting libraries are often based on combinations of the classic Quicksort algorithm with insertion sort applied as base case for small, fixed, numbers of inputs. Unrolling the code for the base case by ignoring loop conditions eliminates branching, resulting in code equivalent to a sorting network. This enables further program transformations based on sorting network optimizations, and eventually the synthesis of code from sorting networks. We show that, if considering the number of comparisons and swaps, the theory predicts no real advantage of this approach. However, significant speed-ups are obtained when taking advantage of instruction level parallelism and non-branching conditional assignment instructions, both of which are common in modern CPU architectures. We provide empirical evidence that using code synthesized from efficient sorting networks as the base case for Quicksort libraries results in significant real-world speed-ups.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Codish, Michael","Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Nebel, Markus E.","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-590763"],"event":{"acronym":"LOPSTR","end":"2015-07-15","place":"Siena, it","start":"2015-07-13","title":"25th International Symposium on Logic-based Program Synthesis and Transformation","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ben-Gurion University of the Negev"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"applying sorting networks to synthesize optimized sorting libraries","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-27436-2_8","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-590763","identifier":[{"id":"84952801978","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-3d267ad4-f252-47b2-a76e-5dd2ad62c6d6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B88328879CCF12E156D3F26E1DEF7E0C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-27436-2_8","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"il","key":"ben gurion university of the negev","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Ben-Gurion University of the Negev","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"codishpau","last":"Codish","name":"Codish, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Markus","key":"nebelpau","last":"Nebel","locid":"4404941b-c94e-417e-83ad-5f01a5ba9db5","name":"Nebel, Markus E.","name_org":"Nebel, Markus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Moreno","key":"falaschipedh","last":"Falaschi","name":"Falaschi, Moreno","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-27436-2_8","eisbn":["9783319274362"],"isbn":["9783319274355"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"127-142","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"25th International Symposium, LOPSTR 2015, Siena, Italy, July 13-15, 2015. Revised Selected Papers","title":"Logic-Based Program Synthesis and Transformation"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84952801978"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3d267ad4-f252-47b2-a76e-5dd2ad62c6d6"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Applying Sorting Networks to Synthesize Optimized Sorting Libraries","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-590763","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Since the proof of the four color theorem in 1976, computer-generated proofs have become a reality in mathematics and computer science. During the last decade, we have seen formal proofs using verified proof assistants being used to verify the validity of such proofs. In this paper, we describe a formalized theory of size-optimal sorting networks. From this formalization we extract a certified checker that successfully verifies computer-generated proofs of optimality on up to 8 inputs. The checker relies on an untrusted oracle to shortcut the search for witnesses on more than 1.6 million NP-complete subproblems.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-626441"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formalizing size optimal sorting networks extracting a certified proof checker","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-22102-1_10","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-626441","identifier":[{"id":"84944674144","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-b9ad4e17-4260-4501-b4fc-7e868c2babb1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1D061C3416008516C3F430A0ED2A2A82"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-22102-1_10","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"urbanpedh","last":"Urban","name":"Urban, Christian","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Xingyuan","key":"zhangpedh","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xingyuan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-22102-1_10","eisbn":["9783319221021"],"isbn":["9783319221014"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"154-169","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"6th International Conference, ITP 2015, Nanjing, China, August 24-27, 2015, Proceedings","title":"Interactive Theorem Proving"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84944674144"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b9ad4e17-4260-4501-b4fc-7e868c2babb1"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Formalizing Size-Optimal Sorting Networks : Extracting a Certified Proof Checker","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-626441","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Frege's theory is inconsistent (Russell's paradox). However, the predicative version of Frege's system is consistent. This was proved by Richard Heck in 1996 using a model theoretic argument. In this paper, we give a finitistic proof of this consistency result. As a consequence, Heck's predicative theory is rather weak (as was suspected). We also prove the finitistic consistency of the extension of Heck's theory to Δ11-comprehension and of Heck's ramified predicative second-order system.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Ferreira, Fernando"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-580935"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the finitistic consistency of heck s predicative fregean system","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84926657639","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-580935","identifier":[{"id":"84926657639","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-1af15f2d-03dc-4065-b863-36241d008847"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-5385717E24CE996734E70393F5406794"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L.","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","name_org":"Cruz-Filipe, L.","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fernando","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","name":"Ferreira, Fernando","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1215/00294527-2835110","issn":["00294527","19390726"],"issn_org":["00294527"],"issue":"1","journal":"Notre Dame Journal of Formal Logic","pages":"61-79","publisher":"Duke University Press","status":"p","title":"Notre Dame Journal of Formal Logic","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84926657639"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1af15f2d-03dc-4065-b863-36241d008847"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Finitistic Consistency of Heck's Predicative Fregean System","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-580935","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Consistency of knowledge repositories is of prime importance in organization management. Integrity constraints are a well-known vehicle for specifying data consistency requirements in knowledge bases; in particular, active integrity constraints go one step further, allowing the specification of preferred ways to overcome inconsistent situations in the context of database management. This paper describes a tool to validate an SQL database with respect to a given set of active integrity constraints, proposing possible repairs in case the database is inconsistent. The tool is able to work with the different kinds of repairs proposed in the literature, namely simple, founded, well-founded and justified repairs. It also implements strategies for parallelizing the search for them, allowing the user both to compute partitions of independent or stratified active integrity constraints, and to apply these partitions to find repairs of inconsistent databases efficiently in parallel.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Franz, Michael","Hakhverdyan, Artavazd","Ludovico, Marta","Nunes, Isabel","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-591529"],"event":{"end":"2015-11-14","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2015-11-12","title":"7th International Joint Conference on Knowledge Discovery, Knowledge Engineering and Knowledge Management","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Active integrity constraints","Implementation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"repairc a tool for ensuring data consistency by means of active integrity constraints","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84960945734","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-591529","identifier":[{"id":"84960945734","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-3fdb78a0-5b3e-4b16-b81c-ace310226ee3"],"keyword":["Active integrity constraints","Database repair","Implementation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-265B57449E5E9B0B10B3E90EE259BCDA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luis","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","name_org":"Cruz-Filipe, Luis","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"franzpau","last":"Franz","name":"Franz, Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Artavazd","key":"hakhverdyanpau","last":"Hakhverdyan","locid":"ce271fdb-b525-429c-96fb-54d886211d71","name":"Hakhverdyan, Artavazd","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marta","key":"ludovicopau","last":"Ludovico","name":"Ludovico, Marta","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Isabel","key":"nunespau","last":"Nunes","name":"Nunes, Isabel","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ana","key":"fredpedh","last":"Fred","name":"Fred, Ana","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan","key":"dietzpedh","last":"Dietz","name":"Dietz, Jan","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"aveiropedh","last":"Aveiro","name":"Aveiro, David","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kecheng","key":"liupedh","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Kecheng","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Joaquim","key":"filipepedh","last":"Filipe","name":"Filipe, Joaquim","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5220/0005586400170026","eisbn":["9789897581588"],"pages":"17-26","publisher":"SCITEPRESS Digital Library","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 7th International Joint Conference on Knowledge Discovery, Knowledge Engineering and Knowledge Management (IC3K2015)","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960945734"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3fdb78a0-5b3e-4b16-b81c-ace310226ee3"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"repAIrC : A Tool for Ensuring Data Consistency by Means of Active Integrity Constraints","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-591529","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Active integrity constraints (AICs) are a form of integrity constraints for databases that not only identify inconsistencies, but also suggest how these can be overcome. The semantics for AICs defines different types of repairs, but deciding whether an inconsistent database can be repaired and finding possible repairs is a NP- or Σ2p-complete problem, depending on the type of repairs one has in mind. In this paper, we introduce two different relations on AICs: an equivalence relation of independence, allowing the search to be parallelized among the equivalence classes, and a precedence relation, inducing a stratification that allows repairs to be built progressively. Although these relations have no impact on the worst-case scenario, they can make significant difference in the practical computation of repairs for inconsistent databases.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-585888"],"event":{"acronym":"FoIKS","end":"2014-03-07","place":"Bordeaux, fr","start":"2014-03-03","title":"8th International Symposium on the Foundations of Information and knowledge Systems","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimizing computation of repairs from active integrity constraints","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/112129486/paper16.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-585888","identifier":[{"id":"84898079811","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-2c5234e9-1055-4863-843a-5b402ea1515c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-02E1375BBE392C139CD73F7FE11E9E0A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/112129486/paper16.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-04939-7_18","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christoph","key":"beierlepedh","last":"Beierle","name":"Beierle, Christoph","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Carlo","key":"meghinipedh","last":"Meghini","name":"Meghini, Carlo","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-04939-7_18","eisbn":["9783319049397"],"isbn":["9783319049380"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"361-380","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"8th International Symposium, FoIKS 2014, Bordeaux, France, March 3-7, 2014. Proceedings","title":"Foundations of Information and Knowledge Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84898079811"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2c5234e9-1055-4863-843a-5b402ea1515c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Optimizing Computation of Repairs from Active Integrity Constraints","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-585888","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Previous work identifying depth-optimal n-channel sorting networks for 9 ≤ n ≤ 16 is based on exploiting symmetries of the first two layers. However, the naive generate-and-test approach typically applied does not scale. This paper revisits the problem of generating two-layer prefixes modulo symmetries. An improved notion of symmetry is provided and a novel technique based on regular languages and graph isomorphism is shown to generate the set of non-symmetric representations. An empirical evaluation demonstrates that the new method outperforms the generate-and-test approach by orders of magnitude and easily scales until n = 40.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Codish, Michael","Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-605748"],"event":{"acronym":"SYNASC","end":"2014-09-25","place":"Timisoara, Timis, ro","start":"2014-09-22","title":"16th International Symposium on Symbolic and Numeric Algorithms for Scientific Computing","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ben-Gurion University of the Negev"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the quest for optimal sorting networks efficient generation of two layer prefixes","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/SYNASC.2014.55","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-605748","identifier":[{"id":"84924253383","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-71c96e92-670b-475e-b2bb-d934c8f1c6e0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0F02ACACB99BF92177CA02CC367498E8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://synasc.ro/2014/%20","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/SYNASC.2014.55","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://synasc.ro/2014/publication/","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"il","key":"ben gurion university of the negev","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Ben-Gurion University of the Negev","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"codishpau","last":"Codish","name":"Codish, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Franz","key":"winklerpedh","last":"Winkler","name":"Winkler, Franz","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Viorel","key":"negrupedh","last":"Negru","name":"Negru, Viorel","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tetsuo","key":"idapedh","last":"Ida","name":"Ida, Tetsuo","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tudor","key":"jebeleanpedh","last":"Jebelean","name":"Jebelean, Tudor","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dana","key":"petcupedh","last":"Petcu","name":"Petcu, Dana","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Stephen M.","key":"wattpedh","last":"Watt","name":"Watt, Stephen M.","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniela","key":"zahariepedh","last":"Zaharie","name":"Zaharie, Daniela","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/synasc.2014.55","eisbn":["9781479984480"],"isbn":["9781479984473"],"pages":"359-366","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 16th International Symposium on Symbolic and Numeric Algorithms for Scientific Computing"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84924253383"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-71c96e92-670b-475e-b2bb-d934c8f1c6e0"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Quest for Optimal Sorting Networks : Efficient Generation of Two-Layer Prefixes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-605748","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This paper describes a computer-assisted non-existence proof of 9-input sorting networks consisting of 24 comparators, hence showing that the 25-comparator sorting network found by Floyd in 1964 is optimal. As a corollary, we obtain that the 29-comparator network found by Waksman in 1969 is optimal when sorting 10 inputs. This closes the two smallest open instances of the optimal-size sorting network problem, which have been open since the results of Floyd and Knuth from 1966 proving optimality for sorting networks of up to 8 inputs. The proof involves a combination of two methodologies: one based on exploiting the abundance of symmetries in sorting networks, and the other based on an encoding of the problem to that of satisfiability of propositional logic. We illustrate that, while each of these can single-handedly solve smaller instances of the problem, it is their combination that leads to the more efficient solution that scales to handle 9 inputs.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Codish, Michael","Frank, Michael","Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Schneider-Kamp, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-640059"],"event":{"acronym":"ICTAI","end":"2014-11-12","place":"Limassol, cy","start":"2014-11-10","title":"26th International Conference on Tools with Artificial Intelligence","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"country":["Israel"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ben-Gurion University of the Negev"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"twenty five comparators is optimal when sorting nine inputs and twenty nine for ten","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ICTAI.2014.36","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-640059","identifier":[{"id":"84944699903","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-e977fcfe-7b0b-4ed8-81f4-35b6c4985d7e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A2A7D00ECAE941F9AD3B5C9A4667AF6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ICTAI.2014.36","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"il","key":"ben gurion university of the negev","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Ben-Gurion University of the Negev","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"codishpau","last":"Codish","name":"Codish, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"frankpau","last":"Frank","name":"Frank, Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Luís","key":"cruzfilipepau","last":"Cruz-Filipe","locid":"44dd7cea-a613-4dfd-9c6d-ac91a0729aad","name":"Cruz-Filipe, Luís","orcid":"0000-0002-7866-7484","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"schneiderkamppau","last":"Schneider-Kamp","locid":"5a2afe33-7a0e-414d-b352-b4b366c08af8","name":"Schneider-Kamp, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-4000-5570","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/ictai.2014.36","isbn":["9781479965724"],"pages":"186-193","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 26th IEEE International Conference on Tools with Artificial Intelligence"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84944699903"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e977fcfe-7b0b-4ed8-81f4-35b6c4985d7e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Twenty-Five Comparators is Optimal when Sorting Nine Inputs (and Twenty-Nine for Ten)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-640059","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Multi-context systems (MCSs) are an important framework for heterogeneous combinations of systems within the Semantic Web. In this paper, we propose generic constructions to achieve specific forms of interaction in a principled way, and systematize some useful techniques to work with ontologies within an MCS. All these mechanisms are presented in the form of general-purpose design patterns. Their study also suggests new ways in which this framework can be further extended.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís","Gaspar, GrąCa","Nunes, Isabel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-641684"],"event":{"end":"2014-11-28","place":"Linköping, se","start":"2014-11-24","title":"9th International Conference on Knowledge Engineering and Knowledge Management","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cruz-Filipe, Luís"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Lisbon"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"information flow within relational multi context systems","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-13704-9_8","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-641684","identifier":[{"id":"84914154525","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-ef13cd8a-84fe-4a2d-a3ff-991721493410"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6CFC6273ACE721766C205F74BA9DF14E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-13704-9_8","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno